          "<p>43.1 <strong>Pricing Autonomy:</strong> The Agent has autonomy to set their own selling prices and margins for travel services, subject to the restrictions and requirements set out in this Section 43 and Appendix J.</p><p><strong>43.2 Net Rate and Family &amp; Friends Vouchers:</strong> Client Travel must not be sold at Net Rate unless a valid Family &amp; Friends voucher is used. Personal Bookings may be made at Net Rate where the Agent is a named traveller and the requirements of Section 44 are met. Each Agent receives two Family &amp; Friends vouchers annually, allowing Net Rate or below-standard-margin sales on two selected bookings per calendar year. The voucher must be recorded against the selected booking. All applicable PTS Trust fees and card-processing fees must be covered in full, including on voucher and Personal Bookings.</p><p><strong>43.3 Monthly Average Commission Margin:</strong> Following the Agent’s probationary period, the Agent must maintain an average commission margin of at least 6%, inclusive of VAT and fees, across bookings made over each calendar month. This is a contractual requirement, not a suggested target. Individual booking margins may vary; the 6% standard is a monthly average and not a separate minimum for every booking. Bookings at 1–2% margins must be kept to a minimum. Pricing training and support are available, but do not replace the requirement to meet the monthly standard.</p><p><strong>Monthly calculation basis:</strong> The 6% standard is a value-weighted gross commission margin, not an unweighted average of individual booking percentages. This basis applies equally to ordinary, high-value and complex bookings. The gross margin remains inclusive of VAT and fees as stated above.</p><p>43.4 <strong>Personal Booking Exception:</strong> Personal Bookings may be made at Net Rate, provided that:<br/>\n- The Agent is a named traveller on the booking<br/>\n- The booking meets the definition of Personal Booking in Section 2<br/>\n- All applicable bank and PTS charges are covered in full by the Agent<br/>\n- The booking is clearly marked as a Personal Booking in the system</p><p>43.5 <strong>Price Lock After Booking Processed:</strong> Once a booking has been Processed (as defined in Section 2), the Agent may not amend the final selling price to the client without:<br/>\n- Issuing an updated invoice to the client detailing the amendments<br/>\n- Providing written communication to the client explaining the reason for the price change<br/>\n- Obtaining client acknowledgment of the price change<br/>\n- Uploading all supporting documentation to The JLT Group's booking system</p><p>43.6 <strong>Price Increase Requirements:</strong> Any price increase must be:<br/>\n- Justified by changes in supplier costs, taxes, fees, or other legitimate factors<br/>\n- Communicated to the client in writing with full explanation<br/>\n- Supported by updated invoices and documentation<br/>\n- Compliant with consumer protection laws</p><p><strong>43.7 Price Reductions After Processing:</strong> Any reduction in a selling price after a booking has been Processed must be supported by an updated invoice and written client communication, with any required client agreement retained in the booking system. The reduction must comply with the monthly-average policy in Section 43.3 and Appendix J, cover all applicable costs and fees, and must not cause financial loss or reputational harm to JLT. An individual booking is not prohibited solely because its margin is below 6%.</p><p><strong>43.8 Detrimental Pricing:</strong> Agents must not price bookings in a way that causes financial loss or reputational harm to JLT, fails to cover required costs and fees, or breaches the applicable monthly-average requirement. A lower-margin individual booking is not, by itself, Detrimental Pricing where it is consistent with the monthly policy and any permitted Personal Booking or Family &amp; Friends voucher arrangement.</p><p>43.9 <strong>Consequences of Pricing Violations:</strong> Breach of this Section 43 may result in:<br/>\n- Formal written warning<br/>\n- Requirement to correct pricing immediately<br/>\n- Forfeiture of commission on the affected booking<br/>\n- Suspension of booking privileges<br/>\n- Termination of Membership for serious or repeated violations</p><p><strong>43.10 Price Matching and Pricing Support:</strong> Price matching is permitted where the Agent retains written evidence of a genuine, comparable offer and the booking does not cause financial loss or reputational harm to JLT. All applicable costs and fees must be covered. Price matching does not automatically waive the monthly-average requirement. Agents should seek support where they are unsure of appropriate pricing. No additional approval requirement arises solely because an individual booking margin is below 6%.</p><hr/>",
